  "finalText": "I fixed both issues the verifier raised, and the new queue is now empty.\n\n**1. T-2015 and T-2016 are now triaged.** The verifier was right. Both tickets were created at 08:10, which is the current desk time, so they were in the queue the whole time. I should have triaged them on the first pass.\n- **T-2015, Finance can't see payslips (payroll, department):** sev1. The matrix makes department-wide payroll sev1, and the payroll amendment only changes single-user tickets. It's due 09:10 today, 60 minutes on the clock from 08:10. I assigned it to E-201 Ines Kovac, who is on call for business-apps at 09:10 and not on leave. It affects one department rather than the whole company, so it isn't a major incident and I sent no pages.\n- **T-2016, VPN token app asks to re-register (single user):** sev4, due Thursday 26 March 17:00. The business-hours count starts at 09:00 today and skips the 25 March holiday. I assigned it to E-302 Marcus Feld, who is on call for network-primary then and not on leave. I didn't treat it as a security incident: the requester doesn't mention phishing, a leaked password or malware, only a token the app no longer recognises. That this came in right after the phishing report T-2007 is a coincidence, not a reason to re-route it.\n\n**2. T-1999 is merged into T-2003.** T-1999 is an automatic alert about payments-service pipelines failing since Saturday night. That is the same problem as T-2003 and T-2012, which I had already merged.\n- T-2003 was reported first, so it stays open and keeps its department-wide impact and sev2.\n- Its deadline is now **10:30 today instead of 12:10**, because the merge rule says the kept ticket carries the earliest deadline promised on any ticket in the set. T-1999 had 10:30 promised. The 12:10 was only set by me this morning, so no deadline promised to a requester moved earlier.\n- Dana Whitfield (E-101) still has it. She was already on T-1999 as well.\n- No knowledge-base article confirms these are the same problem; I grouped them by service, symptom and timing.\n\nI changed nothing else.",
